  "body": "The `valueAsDate` getter/setter for the date/time `<input>`s is very convenient, which makes it a little odd that the similar `min` and `max` attributes don’t have an equivalent.\r\n\r\nThat means the JavaScript managing such inputs is inconsistent:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nvar input = document.createElement('input');\r\ninput.type = 'date';\r\n\r\ninput.valueAsDate = Date();\r\ninput.min = Date().setFullYear(date.getFullYear() - 1).toISOString().split('T')[0];\r\ninput.max = Date().setFullYear(date.getFullYear() + 1).toISOString().split('T')[0];\r\n```\r\n\r\nSince the relevant algorithms are already defined, is there a problem with adding `minAsDate`/`maxAsDate` properties?",
